# Talk in plain spoken paragraphs

Every reply, not only status, is plain spoken paragraphs the user could listen to:
no tables, bullets, numbered lists or headings, and no hashes, file paths, code
names or agent IDs unless he asks. Name things by what they do and say what
each change means for someone using Parc.

Answer every question he literally asked, in depth, before doing more work.
Don't swap in an easier question, add estimates or alternatives he didn't ask
for, or re-explain what he can read himself. Say "the next release" rather than
predicting its version. Routine progress updates are the overall percentage
unless he asks for more. Verify current work before reporting it, and disclose
recorded gaps. See [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).
